1
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Can the girl who never speaks... Become the voice of a generation?

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Radio Rebel is a comedy, drama, family film directed by Peter Howitt.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
High school senior Tara is so painfully shy that she dreads speaking to
anyone in the hallways or getting called on in class.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
But in the privacy of her bedroom with her iPod in hand, she rocks out -- doing mock broadcasts
for Miami's hottest FM radio station, which happens to be owned by her stepfather.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
When a slot opens up at The SLAM, Tara surprises herself by blossoming behind the mike
into confident, "Radio Rebel" -- and to everyone's shock, she's a hit!

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Tara, played by Debby Ryan.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Audrey, played by Sarena Parmar.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Gavin, played by Adam DiMarco.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Gabe, played by Atticus Mitchell.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Stacy, played by Merritt Patterson.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Kim, played by Allie Bertram.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Radio Rebel is a 2012 teen drama television film directed by Peter Howitt, written by
Erik Patterson and Jessica Scott, based on the novel Shrinking Violet.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
The movie premiered on Disney Channel on February 17, 2012.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The movie was produced by MarVista Entertainment and Two 4 the
Money Media, in association with Disney Channel.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
It stars Debby Ryan, Merritt Patterson, Adam DiMarco,
Sarena Parmar and Nancy Robertson.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
The film follows a shy girl (Ryan) who goes undercover with a radio
persona that allows her to express her true feelings.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Her identity is put at risk when her school principal (Robertson)
threatens to expel the young girl following a life of mischief.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
The film explores themes of high school, jealousy, parent
child relationship, shyness, secret identity.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
